<title>GERMANY: Hochtief-Siemens-ABB in Berlin airport bid.</title>
<headline>Hochtief-Siemens-ABB in Berlin airport bid.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction group Hochtief AG said on Tuesday it planned to cooperate in a bid to finance, build and operate the new Berlin airport with Siemens and Swiss-Swedish ABB.</p>
<p>The airport project is to be put out to international tender with the successful bidder expected to be chosen in 1998. It will likely to be Germany's first privately-financed aiport construction project.</p>
<p>Under the private finance model, the airport operators collect revenues linked to usage of the airport and its facilities.</p>
<p>Hochtief, which will be the consortium-leader, is already involved in a similar project in Athens.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
